            "Hermes Lore" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "House Flambeau"
            "Latin" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "insults"
            "Living Language" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "insults"
            "Magic Theory" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Ignem"
            "Parma Magica" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "Mentem"
            "Penetration" SCORE 2 SPECIALTY "Ignem"
            "Stealth" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "entering buildings or rooms"
            "Survival" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "woods"
        }
        SPELLS_KNOWN {
            ^"Palm of Flame" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Ignem" LEVEL 5 CASTING_TOTAL 41
            ^"Pilum of Fire" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Ignem" LEVEL 20 CASTING_TOTAL 41
            ^"Arc of Fiery Ribbons" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Ignem" LEVEL 25 CASTING_TOTAL 41
            ^"Ball of Abysmal Flame" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Ignem" LEVEL 35 CASTING_TOTAL 41
            ^"Circle of Encompassing Flame" TECHNIQUE "Creo" FORM "Ignem" LEVEL 35 CASTING_TOTAL 41
        }
        CHOICES {
            "The Flambeau is very much a one-trick pony. He can throw fire at opponents extremely effectively. His focused Arts and Magical Focus mean that he has some Penetration even for powerful spells. However, he is much weaker if he tries to do anything else. Wrathful and Enemies can be swapped out for other Flaws with no trouble, to break the stereotype a bit, as can his Greater Immunity. He can take another Minor Flaw, and balancing Minor Virtue."
        }
    }

